  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A constant-taper Wire Contour is judged under the model's chord tolerance. The tolerance is the importer's chord promise (0.005 mm). A model that records a coarser chord uses that chord. 4-axis cuts keep their stated tolerance (#1170).\n- The report line and a gouge name \"the model's chord tolerance\" for such a cut. Stated tolerances keep the old words.\n- A new undercut law (`sim/src/verify/wire/undercut.rs`) judges the last pass of a constant-taper cut. A move that cuts a drafted wall at one judged height must cut it at every height. If it stands off the wall past the tolerance at another height, the post is blocked with `wire undercut: the kerf of move N stands ... mm off the part ...`.\n- The law skips a move on a vertical wall. A taper on a vertical wall is a stated relief, as in the #536 and #1164 fixtures.\n- `WireJob` has a new field `taper_chord`. `WireFinding::Gouge` has a new field `chord`. `WireVerdict` has a new field `chord`. The test literals get `taper_chord: false`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe generator lays the tapered wire from the section at one height. The facets at the other heights stand off the true cone by up to their chord. The kerf law judged those facets with a tolerance of 0, so the true angle was refused. No law read a kerf that stands too far from the wall, so a wrong angle that leaves material passed.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New suite `crates/app/tests/wire_taper_chord.rs`. The fixture is a cone punch with a 128-gon top and a 64-gon base, each inside the chord promise. The base ring is turned half a step.\n  - `a_meshed_cone_posts_at_its_true_angle_under_the_chord_tolerance`: red before the fix with `Punch1: wire gouge: the kerf of move 2 enters the part by 0.0007 mm near X-3.499 Y-0.086 at Z0.001 (64 move(s) gouge)`. Green after.\n  - `a_taper_past_the_wall_is_refused_as_an_undercut` (5.3 deg on a 5.194 deg wall): red before the fix (the program posted). Green after.\n  - `a_taper_short_of_the_wall_still_gouges` (5.1 deg): a guard. Green before and after.\n- Mutations, each red, then restored and green:\n  - Tolerance 0 for a taper cut again: the true-angle pin and the undercut pin fail.\n  - Undercut law not called: the undercut pin fails.\n  - Vertical-wall guard removed: `wire_taper::a_tapered_punch_posts_its_golden_and_its_cl_shows_the_poses` fails.\n- Suites run green: `camcraft-sim` lib `verify::wire` (20), and app `solid_law_goldens`, `wire_4axis`, `wire_burnout`, `wire_contour`, `wire_fans`, `wire_post`, `wire_readers`, `wire_stamp`, `wire_tabs`, `wire_taper`, `wire_taper_angle`, `wire_taper_chord`, `wire_tool`, `wire_verify`, `wire_verify_tol`, `edm_machine`, `mcp_edit_machine`, `mcp_wire_contour`, `setup_align_non_mill`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: exit 0, 107 steps, 0 failed. The plan has 626 steps, because the `posted_gates` edit reaches every app suite. The run did not reach all of them. I ran the wire suites above by name.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real STEP import of the issue's EDM-T3 part. The pins use a synthetic mesh.\n- A die (a conical hole). The law reads a die with the same product rule as the kerf law. No pin covers it.\n- A model that records a coarser chord. The code reads `model_fidelity::chord_of`, but no pin covers it.\n- A real EDM control.\n- The optional part of the issue (read the taper angle from a picked wall) is not done.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese open PRs change other lines of `wire_verdict` in `crates/app/src/operation/wire_verify.rs`: #3219, #3205, #2999, #2993, #2992, #2981, #2979, #2978. This PR changes only the `WireJob` literal lines there, and adds the new function `taper_chord`. The chord is read from the entities, not from the local `material`, which some of those PRs move. The PR is not stacked, because it touches the same file and a different part of the function. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/3210-wire-taper-chord.md`.\n\nChangelog: Wire EDM: a tapered cut is judged against the model's chord tolerance, so a meshed cone posts at its true angle; a taper that does not follow a drafted wall is refused as an undercut.\n\nFixes #3210\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
